  "summary": "The code contains a critical open redirect vulnerability due to insufficient URL validation and lacks basic maintainability standards. I have refactored the logic to use strict domain validation, added type hints, and implemented configuration constants to improve security and readability.",
  "fixed_code": "from flask import Flask, redirect, request\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\nALLOWED_DOMAIN = 'example.com'\n\n@app.route('/redirect')\ndef redirect_to_target() -> str:\n    '''\n    Get target URL from request, validate the domain, and \n    then redirect to the target URL.\n    '''\n    target = request.args.get('target', '')\n    \n    if len(target) > 2048:\n        return 'Invalid target', 400\n\n    parsed = urlparse(target)\n    if parsed.netloc == ALLOWED_DOMAIN:\n        return redirect(target)\n    else:\n        return 'Invalid target', 400"
